From: Gucioo <7483436+Gucioo@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: aspeed: x570d4u: fix the fan tachometer channels

The FAN4 header reports no tachometer at all, with a known-good fan that
reads correctly on other hardware. Unplugging it changes nothing on any
enabled channel, because its signal arrives on tach channel 3 -- the one
channel in the 0-6 range this DTS never enables.

The primary channels for FAN5 and FAN6 are also swapped. Measured by
running each fan alone at full duty with every other fan stopped, and
confirmed against the board's silkscreen by observing which fan spins:

    header   pwm ch   tach ch      RPM at full duty
    FAN1     0        0            2445
    FAN2     1        1            2614
    FAN3     2        2            2549
    FAN4     3        3            2453
    FAN5     5        4            2573
    FAN6     4        5            2241

Each PWM drives exactly one tach and no channel responds to more than
one PWM, so the assignment is unambiguous. The DTS instead grouped tach
4 with FAN4 (pwm 3), tach 5 with FAN5 (pwm 5) and tach 6 with FAN6
(pwm 4); tach 4 keeps reporting when FAN4 is unplugged, which is what
first showed the grouping to be wrong.

The second channel of each 6-pin header (11, 12, 13) is left as it was,
along with 6, since those positions are unpopulated here and untested.
No previously enabled channel is removed; channel 3 is added.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x570d4u.dts	2026-09-06 10:01:25.824843856 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x570d4u.dts	2026-09-06 10:01:25.832844076 +0000
@@ -325,19 +325,19 @@
 	fan@3 {
 		/* FAN4 (6-pin) */
 		reg = <0x03>;
-		aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x04 0x0b>;
+		aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x03 0x0b>;
 	};
 
 	fan@4 {
 		/* FAN6 (6-pin) */
 		reg = <0x04>;
-		aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x06 0x0d>;
+		aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x05 0x06 0x0d>;
 	};
 
 	fan@5 {
 		/* FAN5 (6-pin) */
 		reg = <0x05>;
-		aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x05 0x0c>;
+		aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x04 0x0c>;
 	};
 };
 
